FADE IN:

EXT. LIGHTHOUSE - NIGHT #1#

Rain hammers the rocks. A single beam sweeps the black water.

The door at the base of the tower bangs open. MARA (30s, oilskin coat, *soaked*) staggers out with a lantern.

MARA
(shouting)
Dad! Dad, the lamp's failing!

No answer but the wind.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - LAMP ROOM - CONTINUOUS #2#

Brass and glass. The great lens turns, slower than it should. OWEN (70s) sits on the floor, back to the wall, a wrench in his lap.

OWEN
It's not the lamp. It's the clockwork. It always was the clockwork.

MARA
Then we fix the clockwork.

OWEN (CONT'D)
With what? Your mother's hairpins?

MARA ^
If that's what it takes.

[[Consider a beat here before the lens stops.]]

The lens stops.

> CUT TO:

.MEMORY - THE SAME ROOM, YEARS EARLIER

~Turn, little light, turn for the sea,
~Turn till the morning comes back to me.

>THE END<

===

# Act Two

= Mara learns the clockwork.

EXT. HARBOUR - DAY

!SILENCE. The boats rock at their moorings.
